        "object": "<p>Online uproar follows Canadian brand’s use of taiko drum at sponsored festival held to celebrate Chinese culture</p><p>The activewear brand Lululemon has apologised after a promotional event held on the Great Wall of China appeared to mistakenly feature a Japanese drum, prompting an uproar.</p><p>The Canadian-headquartered company, known for its upmarket leggings, has been growing rapidly in China and arranged for a yoga festival to take place in late May on a section of the wall near Beijing.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/jun/17/lululemon-apologises-japanese-drum-great-wall-china-yoga-event\">Continue reading...</a>"
